ave\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r({e}^{2}))-f(r(1)) \\\\  & =f({e}^{2},2)-f(1,0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {({e}^{2})}^{3}-0\\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =2{e}^{6}-0 \\\\  & =2{e}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356161 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356162 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356163 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356164 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356165 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1041 "selection" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356163 13194139535584 true] [17592186356160 1110 #uuid "30603ce0-8680-57a7-ba23-e9bde7ec7852" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356161 1034 "4{e}^{3}" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535584 true] [17592186356161 1111 #uuid "bb0a12cd-b525-559f-bbd3-844e771f946a" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356162 1034 "{e}^{3}-4" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535584 true] [17592186356162 1111 #uuid "159e24eb-e367-55e8-a44f-d43250ae4db5" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356163 1034 "2{e}^{6}" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535584 true] [17592186356163 1111 #uuid "9624a752-ba62-5821-8f54-0c70707823af" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356164 1034 "{e}^{6}-2" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535584 true] [17592186356164 1111 #uuid "0e537f42-e435-5da6-b479-5eaad3cc78cd" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356165 1034 "2{e}^{3}-1" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535584 true] [17592186356165 1111 #uuid "e6667766-5468-5275-a082-6f670331bb81" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356167 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1089 "q-124032" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1100 "Let $f(x,y)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y=2x$ for $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1113 #uuid "8cd02cd8-8b9c-5f00-ab40-0f26ec3c4eea" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356166 1145 "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\nWe start by parametrizing the curve $C.$ A suitable parametrization is\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\frac{t}{2},t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$\n\nThen, the position vectors of the endpoints of the curve are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨0,0⟩, \\\\ r(\\pi ) & =⟨\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r(\\pi ))-f(r(0)) \\\\  & =f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi )-f(0,0) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{e}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356168 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356169 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356170 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356171 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356172 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1041 "selection" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356171 13194139535584 true] [17592186356167 1110 #uuid "f2e12d8b-38bc-5251-a87b-956f47085f8e" 13194139535584 true] [17592186356168 1034 "2{e}^{\\pi }-1